      "text": "At commit `c9e8c2d`, the committed contracts are:\n\n- Per file: **1 MiB = 1,048,576 bytes** for managed configuration and each canonical document.\n- Per resume observation: **8 MiB = 8,388,608 bytes aggregate** canonical context.\n- Default always-loaded context: **16,000 JavaScript characters**—not bytes, tokens, or a semantic-quality measure.\n\nStructural checkpoint validation checks canonical sections, uniqueness, ordering, and recognized headings. Freshness is separate Git evidence: a structurally valid checkpoint can still be stale, and strict `resume --check` must fail when it is. Behavioral continuity is separate again; local tests do not establish cross-harness behavior.\n\nChecks actually run:\n\n- `npm run format:check`: passed; 64 files checked.\n- Focused `tests/continuity.test.mjs`: failed overall, 9 passed/7 failed. Failures arose because sandbox permissions prevented test fixtures from running `git init`; affected behavioral assertions were therefore not verified in this run.\n- Registered Git-diff check: passed, exit 0.\n\nNo files were changed."
